/** \page spec-project-format Project Format

A Marmalade Project by definition is a directory containing a `project.marmalade` file. The general file tree is as follows:

Directories are specified with `[d]`. Hidden files and directories are prefixed with `.`.

```
[d] Project Directory
|-- [d] .marm
|   |-- .gitignore
|   |-- assets.marm
|   |-- packages.marm
|   |-- settings.marm
|   |-- toolchains.marm
|   |-- user.marm
|   |-- [other settings].marm
|   |-- index.marmdb
|-- [d] assets
|-- [d] data
|-- [d] logs
|-- [d] packages
|-- [d] src
|-- project.marmalade
```

\section conventions Conventions

JSON property keys are in `lowerCamelCase`, to match Marmalade's C++ naming conventions.

JSON files should contain the following properties as a minimum:

<table>
<tr>
<th>Key</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`type`</td>
<td>The namespaced type of the file schema. E.g. `Marmalade::Project::Settings`.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`version`</td>
<td>The version of the file schema. Allows automatic migrations when using the `Marmalade::Config` class.</td>
</tr>
</table>

\section marm-dir The .marm Directory

The `.marm` directory contains internal settings for the project. Each .marm file is a JSON file, with the usual `type` and `version` properties.

The name of each file in this directory is specified in the `project.marmalade` file.

\subsection marm-gitignore .gitignore

Contains files that should not be tracked in VCS.

File contents should be:
```
user.marm
index.marmdb
```

\subsection marm-assets assets.marm

Storage of asset UUIDs to their locations. Locations could be on the local file system, or virtual such as when using Marmalade Collaboration services.

When an asset is added to the project, a UUID is assigned and added to this file. That UUID is used wherever this asset is needed to be referenced.

An index is generated in the index.marmdb file automatically.

An example is below. Note that other than the `filesystem` driver, other driver names are not finalised, nor are yet implemented.
```json
{
    "version": 1,
    "type": "Marmalade::Project::Assets",
    "assets": [
        {
            "uuid": "0169a235-dc55-42ba-985f-5a3bf5908f5c",
            "description": "Texture of a teapot",
            "path": "textures/teapot.png"
            "location": {
                "driver": "filesystem",
                "path": "textures/teapot.png"
            }
        },
        {
            "uuid": "3bd00901-035e-487a-96b1-4a5d00c39649",
            "description": "Model for a monkey.",
            "path": "models/monkey.obj"
            "location": {
                "driver": "remote",
                "path": "ftp://myserver/monkey.obj"
            }
        }
    ]
}

Path relative to assets
```

<table>
<tr>
<th>Key</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`assets`</td>
<td>An array of assets in the project. Each object contains the following properties:</br>
    <table>
    <tr>
    <th>Key</th>
    <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
    <td>`uuid`</td>
    <td>The unique UUID identifying the asset.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
    <td>`description`</td>
    <td>The description of the asset.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
    <td>`path`</td>
    <td>The path the asset is 'mounted', relative to the project `assets` directory.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
    <td>`location`</td>
    <td>Location object, containing the driver name and where to find the file.</td>
    </tr>
    </table>
</td>
</tr>
</table>

\subsection marm-packages packages.marm

The schema of this file is not yet planned, but will most likely contain the list of packages, required plugins, and/or bundles, and their required versions.

It will also contain the version of the installed packages, similar to a .lock file used in other package managers.

\subsection marm-settings settings.marm

The schema of this file is most likely to change.

Example:

```json
{
    "version": 1,
    "type": "Marmalade::Project::Settings",
    "productName": "My Project",
    "companyName": "Example Company",
    "description": "A Marmalade project"
}
```

<table>
<tr>
<th>Key</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`productName`</td>
<td>The name of the finished product. As opposed to `name` in `project.marmalade`, this is the name given to built binaries.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`companyName`</td>
<td>The company that owns the project.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`description`</td>
<td>The description of the project.</td>
</tr>
</table>

\subsection marm-toolchains toolchains.marm

The schema of this file is not yet planned.

\subsection marm-user user.marm

Contains local user settings. This is not tracked in VCS.

The schema is not yet planned, but will be of type `Marmalade::Project::UserSettings` and contain properties such as `openTabs`, `currentScene` etc.

\subsection marm-index index.marmdb

A SQLite database for enabling fast lookups. This is not tracked in VCS, and instead generated locally.

There will be an option in the Marmalade UI to regenerate the indices, this will delete this file and generate it again.

The tables and columns of this file are not finalised.

Contains the following tables and columns:

<table>
<tr>
<th>Table</th>
<th>Description</th>
<th>Column Name</th>
<th>Column Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td rowspan="2">`assets`</td>
<td rowspan="2">Index of assets, generated from the `assets.marm` file.</td>
<td>`uuid`</td>
<td>PK. UUID of the asset.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`path`</td>
<td>Virtual 'mounted' path to the asset.</td>
<tr>
<td rowspan="2">`scenes`</td>
<td rowspan="2">Index of scenes, generated by scanning the `data` directory.</td>
<td>`uuid`</td>
<td>PK. UUID of the scene.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`name`</td>
<td>Name of the scene.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td rowspan="2">`entities`</td>
<td rowspan="2">Index of entities, generated by scanning the `data` directory.</td>
<td>`uuid`</td>
<td>PK. UUID of the entity.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`name`</td>
<td>Name of the entity.</td>
</tr>
</table>

\section assets-dir The assets Directory

Contains assets imported into the project, externally edited.

Textures, models, fonts, sounds, videos, etc.

A lot of the files in this directory will be tracked with Git LFS; if they are on the file system at all.

Typically these will be stored in the cloud, and a 'virtual item' will be displayed ('mounted') in the Marmalade project
browser at the `path` in `assets.marm`. The actual file will be managed by Marmalade Collaboration services, allowing
real-time development with artists and programmers.

\section data-dir The data Directory

Objects created inside Marmalade, stored as JSON files, with the filename being the UUID.

These are not designed to be edited outside Marmalade.

Scenes, entities, animation drivers, etc.

\section logs-dir The logs Directory

Logs from running the project. Engine logs are stored globally.

\section packages-dir The packages Directory

Packages vendored into the project directory. This should not be tracked in VCS.

\section src-dir The src Directory

Source code and scripts for the project.

\section global-gitignore .gitignore

Global project gitignore.

File contents should be:

```
packages/
```

\section project-marmalade project.marmalade

This is the file users selected when opening a project. It encapsulates everything to do with the project.

```json
{
    "version": 1,
    "type": "Marmalade::Project",
    "name": "My Project",
    "paths": {
        "assets": ".marm/assets.marm",
        "packages": ".marm/packages.marm",
        "settings": ".marm/settings.marm"
        "toolchains": ".marm/toolchains.marm",
        "user": ".marm/user.marm",
        "index": ".marm/index.marmdb"
    },
    "uuid": "f87f279c-fa5c-4736-b320-000050ff3692",
}
```

<table>
<tr>
<th>Key</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`name`</td>
<td>The name of the project. As opposed to `productName` in `settings.marm`, this is the developer's name of the project, and is never seen by end users.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`paths`</td>
<td>A list of paths to the settings files.<br/>
    <table>
    <tr>
    <th>Key</th>
    <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
    <td>`assets`</td>
    <td>Path to the assets.marm file.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
    <td>`packages`</td>
    <td>Path to the packages.marm file.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
    <td>`settings`</td>
    <td>Path to the settings.marm file.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
    <td>`toolchains`</td>
    <td>Path to the toolchains.marm file.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
    <td>`user`</td>
    <td>Path to the user.marm file.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
    <td>`index`</td>
    <td>Path to the index.marmdb file.</td>
    </tr>
    </table>
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>`uuid`</td>
<td>A unique UUID identifying the project. This is generated on project creation and never changed.</td>
</tr>
</table>

*/
